# fak .worktreeinclude — canonical sparse-checkout policy for detached worker
# worktrees. `fak worktree worker prepare` applies it after checkout (engine:
# internal/dojocal/worktree.go — non-cone gitignore-style include patterns;
# comments and blank lines are skipped).
#
# Semantics: a tracked file is checked out iff it matches ANY pattern below;
# everything not matched is omitted from the worker worktree. Pattern shapes
# verified empirically against git non-cone sparse-checkout (2.55):
#   - unanchored dir patterns ("testdata/") match that dir name at any depth
#     and keep its contents;
#   - root-anchored dir patterns ("/.github/") DO NOT match — use the
#     unanchored form (or a root-anchored glob like "/.github/**") instead;
#   - root-anchored file patterns ("/*.md", "/go.mod") do match.
#
# Excluded by omission (fak#12493 — the reason this policy exists; sizes are
# tracked-checkout approximations):
#   docs/        ~203 MB: docs/research/inventory corpora (jsonl.gz/json),
#                docs data json/jsonl bulk, prose
#   visuals/     ~85 MB: png/gif/mp4/svg media
#   tools/       ~21 MB python tooling;  experiments/ ~12 MB;  l3/ ~2 MB
#   third_party/ ~26 MB vendored C++/CUDA headers (not go-build inputs;
#                the one vendored asset a package embeds is re-included below)
# A worker that explicitly targets an omitted tree (e.g. a docs-lane worker)
# copies this policy into its worktree directory as .worktreeinclude, appends
# the extra include lines, and the engine prefers that file over this root
# policy.

# --- Go source, tests, and Go assembly: every package must build and test ---
*.go
*.s

# --- Module, build, and CI configuration ---
/go.mod
/go.sum
/Makefile
/VERSION
/Dockerfile
/Dockerfile.cuda
/.gitignore
/.gitattributes
/.worktreeinclude
.githooks/
.github/
scripts/

# --- Package-local assets: //go:embed targets and test fixtures ---
testdata/
*.html
*.metal
*.comp
*.golden
*.txt
*.js
internal/**/*.json
cmd/**/*.json
internal/egresslist/lists/
internal/syspromptmmu/third_party/
